---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Cookies" lang="en">
  <article class="prose mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pt-10 sm:px-6 dark:prose-invert prose-h1:text-xl prose-h1:font-semibold">
    <h1>Cookies and browser storage</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted">Last updated: 18 October 2026</p>

    <h2>Does this site use cookies?</h2>
    <p>
      No. hollyhack.org does not set cookies and does not use analytics, ads, tracking pixels or content embedded from other
      services. Fonts, scripts and images are loaded from this domain only.
    </p>

    <h2>What is stored in your browser</h2>
    <p>
      The site stores just two values in your browser's local storage (<code>localStorage</code>), only to remember your
      settings:
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Key</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Kept for</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>theme</code></td><td>your chosen theme (light or dark)</td><td>until you clear your browser data</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>cookie-consent</code></td><td>that you closed the cookie notice</td><td>until you clear your browser data</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      These values are never sent to a server or shared with anyone, and they cannot identify you. Storing information that
      is strictly necessary for a service you asked for (such as remembering your theme) does not require consent under the
      EU ePrivacy rules.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. In exceptional cases Cloudflare may set a technical cookie used only for
      security, for example <code>__cf_bm</code> for bot protection (valid for up to 30 minutes). Such a cookie is strictly
      necessary for the site to work and is not used for tracking.
    </p>

    <h2>How to remove stored data</h2>
    <p>
      You can remove these values at any time by clearing site data in your browser settings. The site keeps working, and
      the theme falls back to your system setting.
    </p>

    <h2>More information</h2>
    <p>
      For details on personal data, see the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. Questions:
      <a href="mailto:kamil@powiem.im">kamil@powiem.im</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
